{"text": "Category H is Intensive Behaviour Intervention or Serious Mental Illness. The educational description is: This category includes students requiring the most intensive, coordinated interventions because persistent behaviour or a diagnosed serious mental illness creates major risk or significantly interferes with learning and participation. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Liam O'Connor, who is in Grade 10 and uses he/him pronouns. Liam has bipolar I disorder diagnosed by a psychiatrist. Episodes of depression and mania substantially affect attendance, sleep, concentration, judgment, and school participation; school and community supports are coordinated. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Liam, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Liam’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-H-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.7125, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "H", "start": 0.725, "end": 1.125, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.1375, "end": 1.3, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Intensive", "start": 1.3125, "end": 1.9, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 23}, {"text": "Behaviour", "start": 1.9125, "end": 2.375, "start_char": 24, "end_char": 33}, {"text": "Intervention", "start": 2.3875, "end": 